       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in delayed puberty:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " boys w ⍉pubertal signs by 14 y may get a 4–6-mo course of ↓dose testosterone (eg, cypionate, enanthate) once a mo; these ↓doses induce puberty w some virilization and don't jeopardize adult height potential; testosterone enanthate (or cypionate/propionate) 50–100 mg IM monthly × 3–6 mo = enough to start pubertal development."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Peds safety (testosterone enanthate label):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " in children, androgens may accelerate bone maturation w.o compensatory linear growth, compromising adult height; the younger the child, the greater the risk; check skeletal maturation (hand and wrist XR) every six mo."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
